  "narrative": {
    "intro": "Raytheon obligated $8.1B in federal contracts in FY2026 to date across 358 awards, with an average award size of $22.7M and obligations down 24.1% year over year. Guided Missile and Space Vehicle Manufacturing is the largest market, accounting for $6.2B in obligations, followed by Ammunition (except Small Arms) Manufacturing at $955M and Research and Development in the Physical, Engineering, and Life Sciences at $567M. Fiscal-year obligations rose from $5.9B in FY21 to a peak of $10.7B in FY25, then moved to $8.1B in FY26 to date. Award activity is concentrated in missile and space manufacturing and related propulsion, electronics, testing, and engineering services. Contract volumes and average award size show Raytheon remains a major prime contractor, while the year-over-year decline of down 24.1% indicates lower obligation pacing in the current fiscal year to date versus the prior year.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "What is Raytheon's federal contracting scale?",
        "body": "Raytheon obligated $8.1B in FY2026 to date across 358 awards, with an average award size of $22.7M. Obligations are down 24.1% year over year. Fiscal-year obligations increased from $5.9B in FY21 to $10.7B in FY25, then were $8.1B in FY26 to date."
      },
      {
        "heading": "Where do Raytheon's federal obligations go by market?",
        "body": "Guided Missile and Space Vehicle Manufacturing received $6.2B in obligations, making it the dominant market. Ammunition (except Small Arms) Manufacturing received $955M, and Research and Development in the Physical, Engineering, and Life Sciences received $567M. Other notable markets include Engineering Services at $133M and Guided Missile and Space Vehicle Propulsion Unit and Propulsion Unit Parts Manufacturing at $123M."
      }
    ]
  },
